 \subsection{ShEx schema validation}
 
-We validated the structural integrity of the knowledge graph using
-Shape Expressions (ShEx), as described in
-Section~\ref{subsec:schema_def}. We defined ShEx shapes for all core
-entity types: sampling sites, soil samples, environmental
-measurements, DNA extracts, sequencing datasets, quality control
-records, and taxonomy observations. We bound each shape to its
-corresponding class instances via a Shape Map.
-
-We implemented the validation using the Apache Jena ShEx library
-(v4.10.0) invoked from Groovy scripts. We integrated ShEx
-validation into the automated deployment workflow: each time the
-workflow regenerates an ABox module, the validation step tests
-instances of the relevant class against their ShEx shape before
-loading the data into Virtuoso. The workflow terminates with an error
-if any instance violates the shape constraints (e.g., a sampling site
